From 79d963a43353c94d258c40d5355675895486a89a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Martin <b@heyomayeah.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 20:25:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 038/110] feat(deacon): read model-escalation.json to promote
 agent on re-dispatch (hq-ko4) (#3530)

When a rig defines .gastown/model-escalation.json, the deacon redispatch
path now reads the escalation rules and passes --agent <to_agent> to
gt sling when the failure threshold is met.

- Add ModelEscalationConfig/ModelEscalationRule types
- Add LoadModelEscalationConfig() (reads <rig>/refinery/rig/.gastown/model-escalation.json)
- Add resolveAgentForRedispatch() (fires rules based on total failure count)
- slingBead() now accepts an agent string and appends --agent when non-empty
- BeadRedispatchState gains LastAgent field to track which agent was used
- Comprehensive tests for config loading, resolution logic, and threshold behavior

Co-authored-by: obsidian <b+git@heyomayeah.com>
Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
